Due to user privacy concerns and the fact that real voice data cannot be desensitized, real voice data is not included in our training process. Instead, we only use the TeleAntiFraud synthetic dataset for training. However, the fraud recognition performance of the trained model on real data has significantly improved, as shown in Table \ref{tab:model_performance}. The accuracy rate has increased from 31.55\% to 73.69\%, the precision rate has risen from 38.89\% to 67.98\%, the recall rate has been substantially enhanced from 35.44\% to 93.00\%, and the F1 score has improved from 37.08\% to 78.55\%. This indicates that the training process has successfully captured the key features of fraud behaviors, enabling the model to function effectively in practical applications and demonstrating its effectiveness and generalization ability. 

