Table\ref{tab:model-performance-total} presents the experimental results of various models under different model types (SenseVoice (ASR) + large language model, multimodal model, fine-tuned anti-fraud speech language model) in terms of different scenario classifications (Accuracy, Precision, Recall, F1 score), fraud-related indicators (Accuracy, Precision, Recall, F1 score), fraud type classifications (Accuracy, Precision, Recall, F1 score), and the average F1 score (Avg F1).

Regarding the SenseVoice (ASR) + large language model, when it comes to scenario classification, the accuracy (Acc) of DeepSeek-V3 reaches 88.53, and its Precision, Recall, and F1 score are all 88.53, indicating a balanced performance. The accuracy of DeepSeek-R1 is 83.13, and its Precision, reaching 84.38, has an advantage. In contrast, the accuracies of Doubao-1.5-Pro, InternLM2.5-20B-Chat, etc., are relatively low, all below 80. In the evaluation of whether it is related to fraud, DeepSeek-R1 performs remarkably well, with an accuracy of 79.98, a Precision as high as 87.22, a Recall of 72.61, and an F1 score of 79.25. By comparison, the accuracies of Doubao-1.5-Pro and InternLM2.5-20B-Chat are 58.59 and 58.46 respectively. In the classification of fraud types, DeepSeek-R1 is also excellent, with an accuracy of 84.65, a Precision and Recall of 86.82 and 84.65 respectively, and an F1 score of 85.16. Among this model type, DeepSeek-R1 has the highest Avg F1 score of 82.67.

In terms of the LALM model, when it comes to scenario classification, the accuracy of Gemini-2.0-Flash is 80.13, and its F1 score of 80.51 shows a relatively good performance. The accuracy of GPT-4o* is 79.26, and its F1 score of 80.25 indicates a considerable performance. In the evaluation of whether it is related to fraud, Gemini-2.0-Flash has an accuracy of 68.61, a Precision of 81.68, a Recall of 46.93, and an F1 score of 59.61, showing an outstanding performance. In the classification of fraud types, GPT-4o* has an accuracy of 87.21, a Precision of 86.07, a Recall of 87.21, and an F1 score of 86.26, performing excellently. Among the multimodal models, Gemini-2.0-Flash has the highest Avg F1 score of 74.55.

For the fine-tuned anti-fraud speech language model (LALM), when it comes to scenario classification, AntiFraud-Qwen2Audio has an accuracy of 80.91, and its F1 score of 81.31 represents a good performance. In the evaluation of whether it is related to fraud, AntiFraud-Qwen2Audio performs extremely outstandingly, with an accuracy of 84.22, a Precision of 86.15, a Recall of 83.45, and an F1 score of 84.78. In the classification of fraud types, AntiFraud-Qwen2Audio has an accuracy of 82.67, a Precision and Recall of 83.57 and 82.67 respectively, and an F1 score of 82.91. This model has the highest Avg F1 score of 83, performing the best among all models, indicating that the fine-tuned anti-fraud speech language model has significant advantages in anti-fraud related tasks.

Different models have their own advantages and disadvantages in different tasks and scenarios. Among them, AntiFraud-Qwen2Audio in the fine-tuned anti-fraud speech language model (LALM) performs the most outstandingly in anti-fraud related tasks, and Gemini-2.0-Flash in the multimodal model and DeepSeek-R1 in the SenseVoice (ASR) + large language model also have good comprehensive performances. 

