To illustrate the effectiveness of the optimal switching strategy, we consider the following baselines for comparison purposes. The results for the total rewards (sum of the immediate reward at each stage and the terminal reward) under different scenarios are shown in Fig. \ref{fig:arbitrage_}.

\noindent\textbf{No switch:} In this case, no switches are allowed; the deception technique remains fixed from the initial stage to the terminal stage. For example, in Fig. \ref{fig:arbitrage_}, case ``0 ($\theta=0$)'' denotes a scenario where the budgeted switch times is zero ($M=0$) and the deception is absent (game mode $\theta=0$). 
