In what follows, we shall often describe finite, loop-free processes using the fragment of Milner's CCS~\cite{Milner89} given by the grammar
$p ::= \mathtt{0} ~\mid~ a.p  ~\mid~  p+p$,
where $a \in \act$. For each action $a$ and terms $p,p'$, we write $p \myarrowa p'$ iff
%\begin{enumerate}[(i)]
