    \item  $B$ plays moves B($\wedge$) and B($\vee$) on $p_i$, for both $i=1,2$, until no formula can be replaced in $L_i(p_i)$.
    If $\bigwedge L_i(p_i)$ becomes unsatisfiable, then $B$ loses.
