\begin{restatable}{corollary}{cornsimeq}\label{cor:twosimul-game}
 Let $U_1,U_2$ be finite sets of $\mathL_{\ell S}$, $\ell\geq n$. Player $A$ has a winning strategy for $\nsimab(U_1,U_2)$ iff for every $p_1,p_2$ such that $p_1\models\bigwedge U_1$ and $p_2\models \bigwedge U_2$, we have that $p_1\curle_{2S} p_2$.
