\old{The applications outlined in this perspective show that certified randomness generated by quantum computers has the potential to generate value in a broad range of domains. Realizing this value requires both hardware and theoretical progress to improve the cost and security of certified randomness generation. Furthermore, the security analysis of the applications may need to be formalized. As a classically infeasible primitive realizable on near-term quantum hardware, certified randomness is a promising early application of quantum computers.}

