For a graph $X$ with $N$ vertices, let $n$, $q$ be a pair of positive integers with $n+q=N$, where $p$ is the number of distinct pebbles and $q$ is the number of unoccupied vertices.
Let $P = \{ 1,2,\ldots, n\}$ be the set of all the pebbles.
