\noindent This $P_f$ we give describes the necessary condition of a decoder: the corrections $r_i(\bs)$ are applied to eliminate all non-zero syndromes on the stabilizers; and weight of corrections should be less than or equal to weight of errors. Alternatively, if we know that $f$ satisfies $P_f$ (e.g., the decoder is given), we can identify $P_c$ by simplifying $P_c^\prime$ without prior knowledge of $P_c$. Instead, if we are aiming to design a correct decoder $f$,
