\begin{equation}
\label{eq:metric1}
S_{\rm IK} = \frac{N_{\rm IK}}{N}, \quad S_{\rm IG} = \frac{N_{\rm IG}}{N}, \quad S_{\rm CM} = \frac{N_{\rm CM}}{N}, \quad S_{\rm RM} = \frac{N_{\rm RM}}{N_{\rm RM}+N_{\rm CM}}
\end{equation}

where \( \text{N} \) denotes the total number of samples and \( N_{IK} \), \( N_{IG} \), \( N_{CM} \), \( N_{RM} \) represents the number of samples for a specific situation. Therefore, we obtain our final reasoning confidence scores:
