\subsection{Details of Data Collection}
\label{subapp:Collection Details}

%%%\chinese{with the pre-defined tree knowledge structure, 我们从各国小学数学考题公开题库中挑选带有图片的几何题目，such as professional exams and practice tests,详细来源见Fig.xx. To ensure comprehensive coverage of fundamental and critical areas in fundamental math, we select the five most foundational and prevalent domains within the field of primary geomatics 基础，包括平面图形、立体图形、图形的变换与运动、位置与方向、测量等五个维度。筛选原则：1. 包含多知识点并且可以按照解题步骤进行拆解2. 题目和图片具有一致性3. 确保正确答案的唯一性和分散注意力的选项具有高度混淆程度。
%题目初筛后，三位专家标注人员对解题步骤进行拆解并标注对应的知识点，对标注结果交叉验证，确保至少两位专家的标注结果是一致的，否则该题目会被视为低质量问题并丢弃。这种高度一致性强调我们标注过程的可靠性和数据的高质量性。
%进行题目初筛后，对解题步骤进行拆解并标注对应的知识点，拆解遵循以下原则：1）每道子题目的解题步骤都必须运用到唯一知识点，不能出现知识点混淆。2）上一道子题目的答案须作为下一道题目的已知条件}%%%
With the hierarchical knowledge structure, we select geometric problems with images from publicly authoritative mathematics websites from various countries, including professional exams and practice tests (detailed sources list can be found in section \ref{data sorce}). To ensure comprehensive coverage of fundamental and critical areas in primary math, we select the five most foundational and prevalent domains within the field of primary geometry, including:
\begin{itemize}[leftmargin = 15pt] 
    \item \textbf{Plane figures}: Questions involving identification and properties of two-dimensional shapes.
    \item \textbf{Solid figures}: Questions related to the recognition and characteristics of three-dimensional objects.
    \item \textbf{Transformation and motion of figures}: Problems focusing on geometric transformations such as translation, rotation, and reflection.
    \item \textbf{Position and direction}: Questions that involve understanding spatial relationships and directions.
    \item \textbf{Measurement}: Problems requiring the measurement of length, area, volume, and angles.
\end{itemize}
The selection criteria are as follows:
(1) The problems include multiple knowledge concepts and can be decomposed into steps for solution.
(2) The problems and images are consistent.
(3) The correct answer is unique, and the distractor options are highly confusing.


