\section{More Details on the Metrics}
\label{sec:Metric}

\textbf{Distinguishing Metric.} Considering the model's instability, Figure~\ref{fig:metric-main} and Figure~\ref{fig:strict-3},~\ref{fig:loose-3} illustrate the two metrics we propose for distinguishing between \textit{RM} and \textit{CM} metrics. Figure~\ref{fig:metric-main} represents the two-step problem, while Figures~\ref{fig:strict-3} and Figures~\ref{fig:loose-3} represent the three-step problem. Specifically, under the strict metric, if there is any error in the corresponding sub-problems of a multi-step problem that is answered correctly, it is classified as \textit{RM (Rote Memorization)}. Only if all corresponding sub-problems are answered correctly (TTTT, TTT) is it classified as \textit{CM (Complete Master)}. Under the loose metric, it is classified as \textit{RM} only if the model answers all sub-problems incorrectly (FFFT, FFT), otherwise, it is classified as \textit{CM}. Therefore, the $\text{Score}_{\text{average}}$ under the loose metric is slightly higher. We hope to see models like GPT-4o~\cite{GPT4o} and GPT-4V~\cite{2023GPT4VisionSC}, which have already performed nearly perfectly under the loose metric and are far ahead of other models, bring us even greater surprises under the strict metric in the next update.

\textbf{Metrics' Intrinsic Logic.} As shown in Figure~\ref{fig:metric-main},~\ref{fig:strict-3},~\ref{fig:loose-3}, it is evident in the Metric for Reasoning Evaluation Section that \textit{IK}, \textit{IG}, and \textit{CM} have a logical relationship. In the early stages of constructing \dataset, we recorded all the model's responses and analyzed the answers to each multi-step problem and its corresponding sub-problems. We believe that for both humans and models, a reasonable learning process should involve first mastering each knowledge concept individually and then learning to comprehensively apply them to achieve complete mastery. The situation where the multi-step problem is answered correctly but the sub-problems are answered incorrectly (\textit{RM}) is an unreasonable phenomenon.
% arises due to the inherent unreliability of the model's training method.
Therefore, we developed a four-dimensional fine-grained metric to further evaluate the model's performance.
% \chinese{如图x-图y所示，在Metric for Reasoning Evaluation部分中可以显然看出IK，IG，CM是具有逻辑关系的。在构建构建wemath的初期，我们统计了模型回答的所有情况，并结合每道多知识点题目与其对应的单知识点子问题的回答情况进行了分析，一个学习过程的合理情况应该是模型先掌握每个知识点，再学会综合运用以此达到完全掌握的情况。而复杂问题回答正确，子问题回答错误的情况（RM）是由于模型的训练方式客观存在的不可靠现象，也因此我们构建出了四维的细粒度metric来进一步评估模型的表现。}



% \chinese{考虑到模型的不稳定性，图x-图y展示了RM与CM指标中我们提出的两种判别标准。其中图x为two-step problems的情况，图y，z为three-step problems的情况。具体而言，在严格的判别标准中，对于复杂问题回答正确的情况，我们认为只要在其对应的子问题当中出现错误，则判为RM（rote-memorizion），相应的只有其对应的子问题全部回答正确(TTT)才判为CM（complete mastery）；而在宽松的判别标准中，只有当模型在拆解的全部子问题均回答错误时（FFFT, FFT），才判为RM，其余情况均判为CM。

% 因此，宽松标准下的score_average会较高一些，我们希望看到如gpt-4o, gpt-4V等模型（在宽松的判别标准下已经接近完美，大幅领先其他模型），在下一次更新的时候可以在严格的判别标准中带给我们更大的惊喜。
