\section{Conclusions} 
\noindent
% We proposed a novel cache placement method for video caching in wireless edge, which considers revenue optimization with estimated file request from transformer prediction under a \ac{fl} structure to protect privacy. The formulated revenue optimization problem can be solved as a 0-1 knapsack problem. Simulation results show the effectiveness of our proposed method compared to other caching baselines. The revenue objective function addressed in this study represents a simplified scenario as discussed in Remark 1. Future research will explore a more comprehensive revenue optimization framework, incorporating the long-term revenue of caching strategies and accounting for the stochastic uncertainties inherent in file request predictions. 
We proposed a privacy-preserving cache placement method for wireless video caching networks using FL-trained Transformers for multi-step content prediction. The predictions, weighted by accuracy and global popularity, optimized cache placement to maximize system revenue. Our  solution outperformed baselines in CHR and revenue. Future work will focus on enhancing revenue optimization by considering long-term caching strategies and stochastic request uncertainties.


