In this section, we present the small-step operational semantics of \cname.
Our rules axiomatize a judgment $\myg \vdash_\epsilon e \evalto{r} e'$ that 
under the loss continuation $\myg$, $e$ makes a transition to  $e'$, producing loss $\ssmathhl{r}\in \R$.
The decorative $\epsilon$ provides auxiliary information needed to construct loss continuations.
Here $\myg$ produces the loss caused by  the rest of
the program, given the result of executing $e$.


