\in X  \to R_\epsilon.\, \eta_{W_\epsilon}(x)$ (and recall that $\eta_{W_\epsilon}(x) = (0,x)$). For the Kleisli extension,
rather than  follow the definitions in, e.g.,~\citet{AP21} via a $W_\epsilon$-algebra on $R_\epsilon$ we give definitions that are a little easier to read. 

